{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ESCALATION — new design decision beyond approved scope (rebar-debug Phase 2, do NOT force)\n\nThe operator-approved predicate `store_is_usable = isdir AND .git present AND\n`git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` resolves` is implemented and GREEN for its own tests, BUT the\nmandated caller-dependency sweep found a SUPPORTED PRODUCTION read path that relies on the old\n`[]`-for-`.git`-less-store behavior and is broken by the approved predicate. Resolving it requires\nCHANGING the approved predicate, which is a new design decision. Holding here per the rule\n\"escalate new design decisions; do not force\". The change is committed LOCALLY ONLY\n(`84237944cedb`) and has NOT been pushed to Gerrit.\n\n== What breaks and why (evidence) ==\n\n`rebar._snapshot.materialize_tickets()` materializes a PINNED, read-only ticket snapshot by\nchecking a git tree out into `<root>/.tickets-tracker/` via a throwaway index — it creates a\ndirectory of event dirs with NO `.git` (confirmed: repo_snapshot.py `_materialize_tree` /\n`materialize_via_donor`; test `test_gate_ticket_snapshot.py::test_materialize_tickets_holds_event_dir`\nasserts only `is_dir()` + event dirs, never `.git`). The code-review GATE AGENTS read this pinned\nsnapshot in production: `LLMConfig.from_env` sets `tickets_path = current_tickets_root()`\n(llm/config.py:623) and the agent's rebar ticket tools (`show_ticket`, `list_tickets`, `next_batch`)\nresolve the store there — funneling through `_reads._tracker`, the exact chokepoint I widened.\n\nBecause a materialized snapshot has no `.git`, `store_is_usable` returns False, so every gate-agent\nread now raises `store_uninitialized` instead of reading the pinned store. This is the MCP AGENT\nREAD SURFACE the approved scope explicitly told me to broaden — it collides with itself.\n\nReproduced directly: a `.git`-less directory of event files\n=> `store_is_usable` = False; `rebar.next_batch(...)` (library/_reads) raises `store_uninitialized`,\nwhile the CLI `next-batch` (a separate read path that does NOT go through `_tracker`) reads it fine.\n\nFailing tests attributable to MY change (6): the 4 `tests/interfaces/store/test_gate_ticket_snapshot.py`\npinned/mirror/ref-chain reads, `tests/interfaces/queries/test_next_batch_compute.py::test_library_and_mcp_shape`,\nand `tests/unit/test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba.py::test_stage_and_commit_git_calls_are_all_timeout_bounded`\n(the last is separately fixable: my new `rev-parse` subprocess needs a bounded timeout on the write path).\nThe other 8 full-suite failures (test_atomic_completion_close x5, test_rebar_repo_isolation x1,\ntest_tracker_footprint_cli x2) FAIL ON CLEAN origin/main too (git `show-ref`/`ls-tree refs/heads/tickets`\n=> 128 in this sandbox) — pre-existing/environmental, NOT my change.\n\n== The irreducible conflict ==\n\nThe ticket's PRIMARY production incident (#1) is a NO-`.git` directory holding `reviewbot-ensure-tickets`\nmarker files that must RAISE. A valid materialized snapshot is ALSO a no-`.git` directory that must\nREAD. They are filesystem-identical except for content: the broken dir has marker files and NO ticket\nevent dirs; the snapshot has ticket event dirs. So a purely `.git`/HEAD-based predicate CANNOT\ndistinguish them — it wrongly rejects the snapshot. The approved predicate as written is incompatible\nwith rebar's supported `.git`-less materialized-snapshot read mode.\n\n== Options (each deviates from the approved predicate — needs operator decision) ==\n\n1. NARROW to the mid-clone case only: `usable = isdir AND (.git present => HEAD resolves)`.\n   Raises on mid-clone (`.git` present, HEAD unresolvable); ALLOWS every `.git`-less dir (snapshots\n   read again). Simple, no heuristic. COST: does NOT fix the ticket's primary incident #1 (no-`.git`\n   marker dir still reads `[]`). Materially narrower than approved.\n\n2. ADD materialized-store detection (RECOMMENDED to satisfy the ticket ACs):\n   `usable = isdir AND ((.git present AND HEAD resolves) OR (>=1 valid ticket event dir present))`.\n   Raises on no-`.git`+no-event-data (incident #1) AND mid-clone; ALLOWS populated snapshots and\n   empty INITIALIZED stores (`.git`+HEAD). COST: a new \"has event data\" heuristic, and an EMPTY\n   materialized snapshot (no `.git`, zero tickets) would raise — operator must rule whether that\n   edge is acceptable (a gate reading a truly empty ticket store).\n\n3. MODE-GATE: skip the usability guard when a pinned tickets root is active\n   (`current_tickets_root() is not None` / resolved tracker == pinned root), keep it for live stores.\n   Exempts production snapshots without an event-data heuristic; still fixes incident #1 (live store).\n   COST: adds mode-awareness to the read chokepoint, and the library-`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`-at-a-bare-\n   event-dir test pattern (`test_next_batch_compute`) would need its store marked pinned or given a\n   `.git` — i.e., decide whether that bare-event-dir library read mode is supported in production.\n\nRecommendation: Option 2 (only option that meets the ticket's stated ACs while preserving the\nproduction gate-snapshot read path), with an explicit operator ruling on the empty-snapshot edge;\nOption 1 as a narrower fallback if incident #1 coverage is negotiable.\n\nI have NOT implemented any of these (that would be forcing a new design decision). Awaiting operator\ndirection on which predicate to adopt. The local commit stays unpushed until then."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787966225663815001,"uuid":"77ab4446-44aa-46ec-9fd9-899c73e56eca"}